        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/pinson/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Louisville & Nashville Railroad ran a line through Pinson in 1889, turning the town into a coal shipping hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/pinson/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Pinson hosts the Pinson Mounds, a prehistoric Native American site that predates the town itself.",
